36
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.140
quarters smaller.

37
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.400
One more expansion creates twenty-seven

38
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.020
size-one leaves. Each costs one

39
00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.760
by the base condition, so

40
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.560
their total cost is twenty-seven

41
00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.700
rather than thirty-six or sixty-four.

42
00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.040
At a general level i,

43
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.820
there are three to the

44
00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.140
i subproblems, each with size

45
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.600
n over four to the

46
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.120
i. Multiplying those quantities gives

47
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.160
n times three quarters to

48
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.540
the i as the total

49
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.140
non-leaf work on that level.

50
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.800
Stop when n divided by

51
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.040
four to the L reaches

52
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.140
one. The depth L is

53
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.520
therefore log base four of

54
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.840
n, and the number of

55
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.160
leaves is three to the

56
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.020
L, equivalently n to the

57
00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.300
